Models downloaded at runtime (not redistributed here):

- Silero VAD v6.2.3 (snakers4/silero-vad) - MIT
- Smart Turn v3.2 (pipecat-ai/smart-turn-v3) - BSD-2-Clause
- Parakeet TDT 0.6B v2 by NVIDIA (nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2; MLX weights mlx-community/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2) - CC-BY-4.0.
  macvoice downloads johnrobinsn/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-mlx-q8, a modified version (bf16, 8-bit encoder)
  made by scripts/make_parakeet_q8.py and published under the same license.
- Phonon 31M English and voice catalog (gradium/phonon-31m-en, gradium/phonon-voices) - Apache-2.0

Optional baseline (the "baseline" extra): Whisper large-v3 and distil-large-v3 (MIT), Kokoro-82M (Apache-2.0).

Test data in tests/fixtures/:

- librispeech/: 20 utterances from LibriSpeech validation-clean (Panayotov et al., 2015), CC-BY-4.0.
- prompts/: speech synthesized with Phonon 31M English (Apache-2.0) by scripts/make_prompt_fixtures.py.
- reference_*.npz: outputs of transformers' WhisperFeatureExtractor and silero-vad's PyTorch model on a LibriSpeech clip, used to pin the NumPy ports.

Parts of the code are adapted from vibr8 (Apache-2.0, same author).
